-- title:
--   Markov property of the path measure for integrable observables
-- statement:
--   **The Markov property of the path measure, for integrable observables.** Let $P$ be a Markov kernel on a measurable space $X$ with invariant probability measure $\pi$, and let $(X_0, X_1, \dots)$ be the stationary chain with kernel $P$ and initial law $\pi$. For every $\pi$-integrable observable $h$ and every time $k$,
--   $$\mathbb{E}\bigl[h(X_{k+1}) \,\bigm|\, X_0, \dots, X_k\bigr] \;=\; \int h \,\mathrm{d}P(X_k, \cdot) \qquad \text{almost surely.}$$
--
--   This is the defining property of a Markov chain, stated for the natural filtration generated by the coordinates up to time $k$: conditioning on the whole past is the same as conditioning on the present, and the resulting conditional expectation is the one-step kernel mean.
--
--   The statement is the extension of the bounded case to observables that are merely integrable, which is what is needed whenever the functional of interest has unbounded range — for instance an influence function that is linear in an unbounded reward. The integrability hypothesis is imposed under the invariant law $\pi$, which by stationarity is the law of every coordinate; invariance also guarantees that $h$ is $P(x,\cdot)$-integrable for $\pi$-almost every $x$, so the right-hand side is defined almost everywhere.
--
--   *Formalization note.* The past is the $\sigma$-algebra obtained by pulling back the product $\sigma$-algebra along the restriction of a path to the coordinates $\le k$.
-- source:
--   Standard; see e.g. R. Durrett, Probability: Theory and Examples, 5th ed., Cambridge 2019, Theorem 5.2.4 (the Markov property), or Galin L. Jones, On the Markov Chain Central Limit Theorem, Probability Surveys 1 (2004) 299-320, §2. The bounded case is the platform theorem MarkovChainCLT.condExp_next_coord; this is its extension to integrable observables by truncation.

import Definitions.Def_MarkovChainPathMeasure
import Definitions.Def_MarkovIterKernel
import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Function.ConditionalExpectation.Real
import Mathlib.Probability.Kernel.Invariance

open Filter Finset Function MeasurableEquiv MeasurableSpace MeasureTheory Preorder
  ProbabilityTheory
open MarkovChainCLT
open scoped ENNReal NNReal Topology

theorem MarkovChainCLT.condExp_next_coord_of_integrable {X : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X]
    (P : Kernel X X) [IsMarkovKernel P] (π : Measure X) [IsProbabilityMeasure π]
    (hinv : Kernel.Invariant P π) (h : X → ℝ) (hh : Measurable h) (hint : Integrable h π)
    (k : ℕ) :
    (fun ω : ℕ → X => ∫ y, h y ∂(P (ω k)))
      =ᵐ[chainMeasure P π] (chainMeasure P π)[fun ω : ℕ → X => h (ω (k + 1)) |
        MeasurableSpace.comap (frestrictLe (π := fun _ : ℕ => X) k) inferInstance] := by sorry
